1. THE FAILING CASE, REPRODUCED (1a): this record's l9t5_case.py imported unchanged on this base
   C-ALLTX rev 3 from its text: 241.039 W at VBAT, need 15.5162 V rest at 18 A (R_cell 0.060 Ohm, the case's ASSUMPTION): +0.0162 V over REQ-018's 15.5 V
   with the printed uncertainties bounded (the BQ4050's uncalibrated 0.8036 A, so 17.1964 A true at the indicated 18 A; the dock's Mill-Max power
   pins at their PRINTED 20 mOhm maximum, +1.0 mOhm over W2's inferred leads and contacts): need 16.0718 V (+0.5718 V)
   the PA's DC input the case allows, the rest unchanged (MODEL): 112.72 W nominal, 103.44 W bounded; today's HIGH is 113.0 W (the 45 W rating
   at the 40 % PRINTED minimum efficiency); the PA stage U13 converts at 0.9844 from VBAT in the budget (the 12 V curve, NOT PLOTTED at 13.8 V)
   so the whole deficit sits in one number nothing in the drawn design bounds: the PA's DC input, today set by an open-loop VGG

2. (a) A1 WITH THE DETECTOR CALIBRATED PER UNIT (the loop holds RF output; the case is judged in DC watts)
