       deviation as TYPICAL only), and board D's U22 reads the PA flange on a lead, not the detector's die: MISSING
     the sampler (coupler) under a field antenna's mismatch: forward-power error +0.42 / -0.45 dB at the sheet's 3:1 stability-row VSWR with a
       20 dB directivity (ASSUMPTION: no coupler is held or designed); calibration into 50 Ohm does not remove it
     the set point and the error amplifier: printable once drawn (small); the detector's supply on board D: the ADL5902 needs 4.5 V,
       over +5V_D8's 4.3408 V floor (record s99a), the ADL5513 runs from 3.3 V on TYPICAL rows only
     THE CONVERSION TO THE CASE'S QUANTITY: the loop bounds RF watts; the case is DC watts. The bounded case allows 103.44 W of PA input, so
       at +-0.25 dB (Pout at most 33.66 W) the PA must convert at 32.5 % or better at that point
       at +-0.50 dB (Pout at most 37.77 W) the PA must convert at 36.5 % or better at that point
       the sheet prints 40 % only at Tcase 25 C, VDD 12.5 V, VGG 5 V, Pin 50 mW (full drive); at VDD 13.8 V under VGG control, hot, no row: MISSING
   VERDICT (a): NOT CREDITABLE at the desk. The calibration's residual (drift curvature, the sampler under mismatch) and the PA's efficiency at
     the controlled point are each bounded by nothing held; a measurement would decide whether the loop holds the case at all (specimen: the
     loop with three RA30H1317M1 on the plate; quantity: the PA's DC input and RF output at the loop's high end, 144 to 146 MHz, flange -20 to
     +85 C, load VSWR to 3:1; limit: DC input under 103.44 W at RF over 30 W). A1 stays a direction, as round 2 left it.

