4. (c) A PA DRAIN-CURRENT LOOP (the module's drain current on the regulated PA rail is the controlled quantity)
   the circuit (drafted in 1c): board A: U13's FB divider at 0.1 %; an INA250A2 (2 mOhm integrated shunt, 500 mV/A) in series between +13V8_PA and J_PA pin 1, on
     +5V_D8IN; a TLV758P as the set-point reference (3.3605 V nominal, 51.1k over 10.0k at 0.1 %); a TLV9062: half A integrates the
     difference, half B inverts it about half the supply, so the output rests at 0 V while the current is under the set point; out on
     J_MEZZ1 pin 16 (AB_SPARE, a spare conductor of the drawn harness) to board D, where a resistor into VGG_FB (U15's feedback node) lowers
     VGG as the output rises. The loop can only LOWER VGG under its open-loop band (4.30 to 4.68 V today): EMCON and the PA's VGG < 5 V
     ratings are untouched; with PA_KEY low U15 is off and VGG stays at 0 V whatever the line does
